  "description": "A Rare Opportunity to Restore a Piece of Irish History.\nAPP Kirrane Auctioneering are delighted to present to the market this truly unique former National School at Driney, Loughlynn, Co. Roscommon.  An exceptional opportunity to acquire and restore a landmark building steeped in local history and character.\n\nOriginally constructed in 1854, this impressive detached eight-bay single storey former National School is a striking example of traditional Irish architecture.  The property boasts a hipped slate roof, cut limestone walls, tooled limestone window and door surrounds, a limestone eaves course, and an elegant pedimented entrance porch bearing the original plaque inscribed \"Loughlynn School 1854\".  Rich in period features, the building stands proudly at the entrance to the avenue leading to the former Loughlynn House and has been recognised by Roscommon County Council as a protected structure, ensuring its historic significance is preserved for generations to come.\n\nAlthough vacant for a number of years and requiring complete refurbishing, this is a blank canvas with enormous potential.  Previous planning permission was granted for redevelopment for a restaurant and one bedroom apartment (now expired), providing an excellent foundation for prospective purchasers to explore a new application, subject to the necessary planning approval.\n\nWith the property vacant for several years, purchasers may be eligible for a range of attractive government incentives, including the vacant property refurbishing grant, the derelict property grant, SEAI home energy upgrade grant, together with grants towards eligible windows and doors, subject to meeting the relevant terms and conditions. \n\nPositioned just off the main road in a peaceful countryside sitting, the property enjoys excellent accessibility while offering privacy and tranquillity.  It is conveniently located within easy driving distance of Loughlynn, Tulsk, Ballyhaunis, Ireland West Airport, Knock Shrine and Castlerea, making it an ideal location for those seeking country living without sacrificing convenience. \n\nWhether you dream of creating an exceptional family residence, a distinctive countryside retreat, or breathing new life into a cherished local landmark, this remarkable property offers endless possibilities for the discerning buyer with vision.\n\nOpportunities to acquire buildings of such historical importance and architectural charm are increasingly rare.  For further information or to arrange a viewing please contact the Sole Selling Agents APP Kirrane Auctioneering - where everything we touch turns to SOLD.\n\nPlease Note: These particulars are for general information only for this property. The details contained are not to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. Whilst every care is taken in the preparation of the property details, neither APP Kirrane Auctioneering or the vendor accept any liability for the details contained in the description of the property. The interested persons must satisfy themselves by viewing the property or employ somebody to inspect the property on their behalf. No Auctioneer or Staff Member employed by APP Kirrane Auctioneering in either; Main Street, Ballyhaunis, Co. Mayo or Bohermore, Galway has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property.",
